{"text": "ALESIA \u00a5. WILKINS-BRAXTON\n\nBoBBY JINDAL\n\u2018ACTING-PRESIDENT\n\nGOVERNOR\n\nLouisiana Housing Finance Agency\n\nOctober 13, 2011\n\nInternal Revenue Service\nAttn: Grace Robertson, C7-226\n5000 Ellin Road,\nLanham, MD 20706\n\nCornerstone Homes has not been able to be placed back in commerce since hurricane Katrina,\n\u2018The project has not been able to produce any viable plan to be brought back online. They have\nmentioned recently , that they are waiting on some funding from the City of New Orleans, but could\nnot produce any supporting documentation of such funding. When we monitored the project in 2009,\nit was being rehabbed and it appeared to be headed back online. During a recent follow up it became\napparent that all remodeling and rehabilitation work had stopped. We contact the owner Pastor\nSouthall (w/ Cornerstone Homes of New Orleans, LLC) who stated they had run out of funds for\ncompletion of repairs. Since the project is not providing housing and/or able to give verifiable\ndocumentation of coming back, we are issuing an 8823.\n\nyi pee ca\n\nRicky Patterson\nCompliance Supervisor, LHFA\n\ne-mail: rpatterson@Ihfa.state.la.us\nphone #t: 225-763-8700 Ext. 303",
